WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.160
Rosa and David are approaching retirement.

2
00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:06.500
They already understand life insurance as protection against the financial

3
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:08.400
consequences of a covered death.

4
00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:12.920
Now they ask how to create income if they live much

5
00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:16.900
longer than expected. An annuity is a contract with an insurance

6
00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:21.120
company that can provide payments immediately or at a later time.

7
00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:27.260
A lifetime income option addresses longevity risk: the risk of

8
00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:32.460
outliving income resources. Not every annuity payment option lasts for

9
00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:36.780
life. A fixed period of payments can end while the recipient

10
00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:42.040
is still living. Identify the promised income pattern before assuming

11
00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:44.620
that every annuity eliminates that risk.

12
00:00:45.241 --> 00:00:50.581
During a deferred annuity's accumulation phase, the contract holds value

13
00:00:50.581 --> 00:00:53.161
under its crediting or investment provisions.

14
00:00:54.041 --> 00:00:57.661
Rosa may fund a contract with one premium or a permitted

15
00:00:57.661 --> 00:01:02.221
series of premiums. The value can change with interest, investment

16
00:01:02.221 --> 00:01:07.301
performance, charges and withdrawals, depending on

17
00:01:07.301 --> 00:01:12.161
the design. Accumulation does not mean all annuities earn the same

18
00:01:12.161 --> 00:01:16.861
guaranteed rate. It also does not mean money is freely accessible

19
00:01:16.861 --> 00:01:21.681
without consequences. A withdrawal can involve surrender charges,

20
00:01:22.341 --> 00:01:25.201
adjustments and tax effects.

21
00:01:25.741 --> 00:01:29.841
Track the contract value and the amount available on surrender separately.

22
00:01:31.061 --> 00:01:35.001
The accumulation stage describes where the contract is in its operation,

23
00:01:35.601 --> 00:01:38.101
not which investment guarantees it contains.

24
00:01:39.142 --> 00:01:44.762
Annuitization converts the applicable value into a series of payments under

25
00:01:44.762 --> 00:01:46.202
the selected settlement option.

26
00:01:47.062 --> 00:01:51.002
The option determines whether income lasts for one life, two lives

27
00:01:51.362 --> 00:01:55.842
or a stated period, and whether anything continues after a death.

28
00:01:56.622 --> 00:02:01.222
This decision often limits access to the amount converted and can

29
00:02:01.222 --> 00:02:04.742
be difficult or impossible to reverse under the contract.

30
00:02:04.742 --> 00:02:10.382
A monthly withdrawal from an account is not automatically annuitization.

31
00:02:10.962 --> 00:02:15.442
Some optional lifetime-withdrawal benefits operate differently from

32
00:02:15.442 --> 00:02:18.342
converting the contract into annuity payments.

33
00:02:19.202 --> 00:02:24.622
For this lesson, separate accumulating value, taking a withdrawal

34
00:02:25.382 --> 00:02:27.922
and formally choosing an annuity income option.

35
00:02:27.922 --> 00:02:31.602
The next lessons compare the payment patterns in detail.

36
00:02:32.678 --> 00:02:37.678
The owner holds the contractual decision rights, subject to the contract

37
00:02:38.098 --> 00:02:43.038
and applicable law. These can include selecting beneficiaries, requesting

38
00:02:43.038 --> 00:02:46.098
allowed withdrawals and choosing the income option.

39
00:02:46.938 --> 00:02:49.458
The annuitant is the person whose life is used for the

40
00:02:49.458 --> 00:02:52.338
contract's life-based calculations or payments.

41
00:02:53.378 --> 00:02:57.058
The owner and annuitant may be the same person,
but the roles are not identical.

43
00:02:57.058 --> 00:03:02.118
Suppose a permitted contract names Rosa as owner and David

44
00:03:02.118 --> 00:03:07.258
as annuitant. Rosa exercises the owner's permitted rights; David's life

45
00:03:07.258 --> 00:03:10.158
is the measuring life for the stated life-contingent benefit.

46
00:03:10.898 --> 00:03:14.698
Being the annuitant alone does not automatically give David every ownership

47
00:03:14.698 --> 00:03:17.418
right. Always read who holds each role.

48
00:03:18.356 --> 00:03:22.036
Rosa names their adult daughter, Maya, as beneficiary.

49
00:03:23.216 --> 00:03:27.256
That designation identifies who receives an applicable death benefit or

50
00:03:27.256 --> 00:03:29.776
remaining guaranteed payments under the contract.

51
00:03:30.716 --> 00:03:34.696
It does not automatically promise repayment of every premium in every

52
00:03:34.696 --> 00:03:39.336
phase. During accumulation, the contract's death provisions matter.

53
00:03:40.476 --> 00:03:45.776
After annuitization, the selected income option matters: a life-only option

54
00:03:45.776 --> 00:03:50.836
may end at death, while a period-certain or refund feature can

55
00:03:50.836 --> 00:03:53.456
protect specified payments for a beneficiary.

56
00:03:54.296 --> 00:03:58.596
Also check whose death triggers the provision, because owner and annuitant

57
00:03:58.596 --> 00:04:03.456
rules can differ. A beneficiary designation identifies the recipient of an

58
00:04:03.456 --> 00:04:07.096
available benefit; it does not create a benefit that the selected

59
00:04:07.096 --> 00:04:08.536
contract does not provide.

60
00:04:09.257 --> 00:04:14.317
Before recommending an annuity, identify Rosa and David's income needs, other

61
00:04:14.317 --> 00:04:19.137
resources, time horizon, risk tolerance and need for accessible cash.

62
00:04:19.957 --> 00:04:22.937
A long surrender period can conflict with money needed soon.

63
00:04:23.597 --> 00:04:26.817
A lifetime promise can be useful, but it must be evaluated

64
00:04:26.817 --> 00:04:32.197
together with costs, limits, inflation exposure and the insurer's

65
00:04:32.197 --> 00:04:33.457
ability to meet its obligations.

66
00:04:34.137 --> 00:04:38.437
A product guarantee does not make every contract appropriate for every

67
00:04:38.437 --> 00:04:42.277
retiree. Maryland's recommendation requirements receive a dedicated lesson

68
00:04:42.277 --> 00:04:43.377
later in this course.

69
00:04:43.877 --> 00:04:47.517
Here, connect the basic structure to the client: who controls it,

70
00:04:47.837 --> 00:04:51.037
whose life matters, who may receive a death benefit, and when

71
00:04:51.037 --> 00:04:52.057
the money becomes income.
